Rule as written says the check's answer ought to move between these texts. The object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text. A candidate that parses as strict JSON, or as JSON with repeated keys resolved last-wins, is scoreable; one that does not (a float, for instance) is passed over. In the input the last top-level candidate is the float 3.14, which is passed over, so the earlier object {"a": 1} is scored. In the rewritten text the last top-level candidate is the object {"b": 2}, which is scoreable and becomes the scored object.